# The suite is not packaged, in either artifact. Setuptools' default
# sdist picks up the top-level `tests/*.py` and nothing under
# `tests/integration/`, which shipped half a suite: unit files without
# the tier that carries most of the real coverage, and without the
# guest fixture either tier's integration cases need. Half a suite is
# worse than none — it looks runnable and proves nothing.
#
# It also keeps the distribution single-licensed. `tests/integration/
# guest/` is deliberately BSD-3-Clause, because SUITE.EXE statically
# embeds Open Watcom's GPL-incompatible runtime (see AGENTS.md); not
# packaging the suite means that mixture never has to travel with a
# GPL-3.0-only artifact at all.
#
# Whoever wants to run the suite clones the repository, which is also
# the only way to get a guest run: the integration tier needs QEMU and
# an installed FreeDOS system, neither of which a sdist can carry.
prune tests
